    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|>But steps toward what? even when I try to take those \"steps,\" I just end up back at zero. it feels like no matter how much I fight, the outcome is always the same. it's like trying to run a race where the finish line keeps moving further away. i'm just... i'm so worn out by the constant effort for nothing. what's even the point of trying to fix something that's fundamentally broken?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is utterly draining when effort feels futile, and you are right to feel tired. Instead of focusing on \"fixing\" something, perhaps the goal could be to simply observe the loop without judgment. Sometimes the point isn't a perfect finish line, but learning to be kinder to yourself *within* the cycle. You deserve rest from the constant pressure to succeed.",
      "source": "target",
